What is @RestControllerAdvice?
It’s a Spring annotation that allows you to handle exceptions globally for all REST controllers in a consistent way.

Difference between @ControllerAdvice and @RestControllerAdvice?
| `@ControllerAdvice`            | `@RestControllerAdvice`   |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------- |
| Used for web MVC (views)       | Used for REST APIs (JSON) |
| Returns ModelAndView           | Returns JSON body         |
| Needs `@ResponseBody` manually | Automatically includes it |

Why use ResponseEntity?
It lets you return both body and HTTP status code together, e.g.
ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body(errorObject);

How does Spring find which @ExceptionHandler to use?
It looks for the closest match — first local (in controller), then global (@ControllerAdvice).

What’s the advantage of global handling?
Centralized logic, cleaner controllers, consistent API responses.